{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01TjiJBZbXhghpSU1fG7f9PV","type":"tool_result","content":"141:    - \"node-conditions\"\n142:    - \"ready-condition\"\n295:The shape is the more interesting thing, though. You have been typing commands in exactly this form since Chapter 4 (`kubectl apply -f`, `kubectl get pods`, `kubectl scale`) and nobody has told you what the form *is*. It worked anyway. That is precisely the condition under which a candidate walks into the exam room confident and then loses five points to a question about which component is permitted to be one minor version newer than which.\n679:[Omitted long matching line]\n681:### Node conditions\n683:A Node's status contains Addresses (HostName, ExternalIP, InternalIP); Conditions; Capacity and Allocatable; and Info such as kernel version, container runtime and kubelet version [source: k8s-docs-nodes-2026-08-23]. `kubectl describe node <name>` shows them [source: k8s-docs-nodes-2026-08-23].\n685:The conditions describe the status of all Running nodes [source: k8s-docs-nodes-2026-08-23]:\n687:| Condition | True when |\n695:*(All five conditions and the three `Ready` values: [source: k8s-docs-nodes-2026-08-23].)*\n703:[Omitted long matching line]\n\n[Showing results with pagination = limit: 10]"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"a6100e90-d251-4659-a972-faa45e77104d","uuid":"f986348a-3386-4371-88bf-c296048d9707","timestamp":"2026-08-25T02:02:56.137Z","tool_use_result":{"mode":"content","numFiles":0,"filenames":[],"content":"141:    - \"node-conditions\"\n142:    - \"ready-condition\"\n295:The shape is the more interesting thing, though. You have been typing commands in exactly this form since Chapter 4 (`kubectl apply -f`, `kubectl get pods`, `kubectl scale`) and nobody has told you what the form *is*. It worked anyway. That is precisely the condition under which a candidate walks into the exam room confident and then loses five points to a question about which component is permitted to be one minor version newer than which.\n679:[Omitted long matching line]\n681:### Node conditions\n683:A Node's status contains Addresses (HostName, ExternalIP, InternalIP); Conditions; Capacity and Allocatable; and Info such as kernel version, container runtime and kubelet version [source: k8s-docs-nodes-2026-08-23]. `kubectl describe node <name>` shows them [source: k8s-docs-nodes-2026-08-23].\n685:The conditions describe the status of all Running nodes [source: k8s-docs-nodes-2026-08-23]:\n687:| Condition | True when |\n695:*(All five conditions and the three `Ready` values: [source: k8s-docs-nodes-2026-08-23].)*\n703:[Omitted long matching line]","numLines":10,"totalLines":23,"appliedLimit":10}}
